  "logline": "An angel from the future is sent to Earth on a holy mission: find the saint, the sacrificial lamb, and write a scroll.",
  "synopsis": [
    "A young postman sorting lost mail opens a letter from an author who claims to be an angel from the future. In its pages, the fallen angel Mott tells his story.",
    "Through a series of cryptic phone calls, an unknown entity gives Mott three tasks to complete before the next Sabbath, when the world will end: find the saint who does not know he is holy; find the sacrificial lamb and offer its blood; and write a scroll recording everything he sees.",
    "His journey takes him through London and Bucharest. As he attempts to fulfil his master’s wishes, Mott becomes disillusioned with his mission and longs to become human, even if it means giving up his immortality. But who is the author, and how much of his story can be believed? It falls to the postman to get Mott’s message to its intended destination."
  ],
